## Usage

```bash
pulumi config set --secret dbPassword '...' -s prod   # sets encrypted secret
pulumi up -s dev    # dev is independent; prod state untouched
pulumi up -s prod
```

## How acceptance criteria are met

| Criterion | Implementation |
|---|---|
| Bucket versioning + encryption, no public access | `versioning.enabled`, SSE-KMS, full `BucketPublicAccessBlock` |
| RDS deletion protection, 7-day backups, private | hardcoded `deletionProtection: true`, `backupRetentionPeriod: 7`, `publiclyAccessible: false` |
| Secret never plaintext | `requireSecret` → Pulumi-encrypted config + secret `Output` |
| Least privilege, no wildcards | OIDC trust pinned to one SA; actions enumerated, resources scoped to bucket |
| Env isolation | separate `Pulumi.dev.yaml` / `Pulumi.prod.yaml`, independently deployable |

Two deliberate design points: deletion protection and backup retention are **not** configurable per stack — the spec requires them in all environments, so the component enforces them. And the connection string `Output` is marked secret and intentionally not exported, so it never renders in plaintext stack outputs.
